      "writtenOn": "2024-07-16T22:17:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct me if I\u0027m wrong: is the issue here that `ctx.DeviceConfig().DeviceArch()` will be the empty string for host contexts, and therefore the conditional will be perpetually true and will always skip?\n\nAnd the behavior we want for host contexts is the proposed \"arbitrary fallback\", which can be achieved by your suggestion?",
      "parentUuid": "ce795cd8_a171fa1c",
      "revId": "220b4abfc814fcff89134fbb1b9015cdeed26d72",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "09fa1903_aa62a086",
        "filename": "cc/ccdeps.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 187,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-16T22:19:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, `DeviceArch()` just returns the global config for the architecture configured for the device.  For physical devices it will generally be `arm64`, for cuttlefish it will generally be `x86_64`.  The host is always `x86_64` though, which is sometimes mistaken as matching `DeviceArch()`.  You should check `ctx.Device() \u0026\u0026 ctx.Arch() \u003d\u003d ctx.DeviceConfig().DeviceArch()`.\n\nFor modules that don\u0027t have anything that matches that check, you should take the first variant seen.",
      "parentUuid": "388460ba_2bb05d40",
      "revId": "220b4abfc814fcff89134fbb1b9015cdeed26d72",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
